  "_meta": {
    "version": 1,
    "updated": "2026-07-10",
    "research_notes": "Funnel order mirrors how media planners actually filter: (1) GEO first \u2014 budgets are prioritized by market (state/DMA) before anything else, because location decides where investment concentrates and DMAs are the historical unit of media buying; (2) DEMOGRAPHIC second \u2014 age (x gender/language) splits within each market, matching the platform layer where targeting lives (Meta/TikTok ad sets, Google ad groups); (3) TASTE third \u2014 music/interest affinity is the leaf, the psychographic layer platforms expose as interest/affinity/genre targeting. Every impression lands in exactly one leaf = (market x age band x taste cluster), and every leaf gets a scored music brief \u2014 geo pack re-flavors the taste cluster's direction, so a hip-hop 18-24 leaf sounds like trap in Atlanta and drill in New York. COMPLIANCE: race/ethnicity is NOT a targetable attribute on any major platform; the compliant proxies this tree uses are age, geography, language-market, and music-culture affinity. State populations are approximate 2020 US Census figures (millions); age-band total_pop_share values approximate the US age structure (18-65 is ~77% of total population), so addressable-population estimates are people-honest. Used only for budget/reach weighting.",
    "sources": [
      "https://tinuiti.com/blog/ecommerce/geotargeting/",
      "https://journalism.university/advertising-and-public-relations/step-by-step-guide-effective-media-plans/",
      "https://lwdirect.com/news/how-to-use-audience-segmentation-for-targeted-tv-campaigns/",
      "https://www.adstellar.ai/blog/guide-to-meta-ads-campaign-structure",
      "https://telmarhelixa.com/resources/audience-segmentation",
      "https://www.census.gov/library/stories/state-by-state.html"
    ]
  },
  "funnel": [
    {
      "level": "geo",
      "label": "Market",
      "why": "Media buys are prioritized by market first (state/DMA); geography decides budget concentration and is the coarsest platform targeting unit."
    },
    {
      "level": "age",
      "label": "Demographic",
      "why": "Age bands are the universal demographic split every platform targets natively; gender/language layer on top where policy allows."
    },
    {
      "level": "taste",
      "label": "Taste cluster",
      "why": "The leaf: music-culture affinity, expressed on-platform as interest/affinity/genre targeting. This is where the score is personalized."
    }
  ],
